    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "THE SCALING PROBLEM",
      "narration_text": "Bigger models perform better — that pattern has held for years. But in a dense transformer, every token activates every parameter. A seven-billion-parameter model does seven billion operations per token. Scale to seventy billion and the compute bill scales with it. The parameters are the compute. So the question becomes: does every token really need every parameter, or could most of them sit this one out?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "build",
