    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "WHY IT WORKS",
      "narration_text": "This is why the largest open models use Mixture of Experts. You can scale a model's total knowledge — its parameter count — without proportionally scaling the cost of running it. A model with a hundred and forty billion total parameters that activates only thirty-nine billion per token can match or outperform a dense seventy-billion-parameter model at roughly half the inference cost. Massive capacity, sparse compute. That's the tradeoff MoE unlocks.",
